- I do this.
- And I'm like,

00:08:19.489 --> 00:08:21.532
what is food? What is food preparation?

00:08:21.532 --> 00:08:23.790
What is planning? What's
the approach here?

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:25.920
Just someone to just
remind me that it's coming.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:27.802
- I'm bad at that too.
I think you're too busy.

00:08:27.802 --> 00:08:29.940
- Yeah, exactly. I get like
wrapped up in something.

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:31.852
- Yeah, yeah.
- And you're hungry.

00:08:31.852 --> 00:08:34.117
And then, I mean, if we're in
a world where we're dreaming,

00:08:34.117 --> 00:08:35.871
it's also preparing the food for me.

00:08:35.871 --> 00:08:36.704
(audience laughing)

00:08:36.704 --> 00:08:38.640
Because even sometimes
when you're that hungry,

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:40.746
like a mac and cheese seems
kind of insurmountable.

00:08:40.746 --> 00:08:41.820
- [Kelly] Yes.
- Yes.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:42.960
- It's hilarious to me

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:44.513
how many cooking demos I do on this show.

00:08:44.513 --> 00:08:45.443
- [Allison] I know.
- And I'm not a cook.

00:08:45.443 --> 00:08:48.960
- I know. I know.
- It's ironic. Really.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.150
- I relate to you in that way.
- Oh yeah. Me too.

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:53.310
So wait so you'll have to
start making kid movies though

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:54.585
because, so when I started having kids,

00:08:54.585 --> 00:08:56.705
I started doing, like I wrote books,

00:08:56.705 --> 00:08:59.310
I like started quilting, I
started doing all these things

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:00.143
that I never thought I'd do.

00:09:00.143 --> 00:09:01.080
- No, I haven't entered that stage yet.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:03.180
- They're not good.
They're not great quilts.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:06.919
Don't look closely. Don't look closely.

00:09:06.919 --> 00:09:08.070
But I started doing things

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:09.870
that were like different
for me in general.

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:12.330
And reaching one?

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:13.980
- Just turned, yeah
he's a little over one.

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:15.270
- [Kelly] That's exciting.
- Thank you.

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:18.039
- Yeah, so what is it like?
What do you think mother,

00:09:18.039 --> 00:09:20.850
I think motherhood totally,
it doesn't change you,

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:21.690
you still have your identity,

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:24.180
but it does bring different
parts of you out, I feel like.

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:26.820
- Oh yeah. There's no part
of it that I was like,

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:28.382
I nailed that in my anticipation.

00:09:28.382 --> 00:09:29.790
(Kelly laughing)

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:31.140
I knew exactly what that would be like.

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:32.910
Like from the beginning
of the whole experience,

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:34.020
all of it is surprising.

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:36.240
But I have found it to be,

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:39.480
I don't know, I get
really shy, first of all,

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:40.980
talking about, I don't know why,

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:42.549
I feel like shy talking about it.

00:09:42.549 --> 00:09:43.965
- Oh that's okay.
- It's this new part of me

00:09:43.965 --> 00:09:45.810
I like haven't figured out how to assess.

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:47.156
I kind of want to wait a
couple years and be like,

00:09:47.156 --> 00:09:48.967
what do you think of me?

00:09:48.967 --> 00:09:52.260
How am I doing?
- Yeah, ask the kid.

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:53.272
- Yeah, could you write an evaluation?

00:09:53.272 --> 00:09:54.412
- Did I do all right?

00:09:54.412 --> 00:09:55.800
- What do you think of my service?

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:57.780
They have the little like
smiley faces in hospitals.

00:09:57.780 --> 00:09:59.490
- One to five.
- Yeah, exactly.

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:01.830
No, it's changed every
part of me, I think.

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:03.416
- One is, that's still really young.

00:10:03.416 --> 00:10:05.730
Like you're still kind of like
going through the motions.

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:06.563
You're sleeping though, right?

00:10:06.563 --> 00:10:08.820
- Yeah, yeah, yeah. We got that.

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:10.740
- That's the hardest part is like,

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:11.820
somebody told me about sleep training

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:13.740
and it saved me.
- [Allison] Did that.

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:15.000
- Especially for working parents.

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:16.890
- Yes very hard. You gotta have sleep.

00:10:16.890 --> 00:10:18.720
- If you weren't an actress,

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:20.580
also if you just wanna do on the side,

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:23.100
you would be an amazing comedian.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:25.293
Your timing is so funny.
Your comedic timing.

00:10:25.293 --> 00:10:27.237
(audience clapping)
- That's so nice. Thank you.

00:10:27.237 --> 00:10:28.860
- I'm like laughing this whole interview.

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:30.630
I was like, she's really funny.

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:33.245
- I feel the same way about,
I'm so happy you're doing this.

00:10:33.245 --> 00:10:34.257
- [Kelly] Oh, thank you.

00:10:34.257 --> 00:10:35.752
- You are made to do a lot
of things in this world.

00:10:35.752 --> 00:10:36.883
(audience clapping)
This is one of them.

00:10:36.883 --> 00:10:38.550
- Thank you. I enjoy it.

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:39.900
But I'm just saying, you're hilarious.

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:41.557
We're gonna stop for a quick break though.

00:10:41.557 --> 00:10:42.870
"M3gan" is in theaters now.

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:44.670
If you like to be scared, go see it.

